{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["And the verse's saying <b>to the inhabitant, etc. they heard, etc.</b> One needs to know what they will say to the inhabitants of the land. And if his intention is to say that they will say it is because of lack of power in HaShem, perish the thought, to help them, then he should have joined the matters in this manner: ״to the inhabitant, etc. because of lack of power in HaShem,״ and he should have placed the statement ״they heard,״ etc. either before or after." "<b>However,</b> the intention of the statement is in this manner: <b>and they will say,</b> etc. — meaning, when Egypt hears, they will attribute the matter to the merit of the inhabitants of the land, meaning it was because of them. And since there are here two paths: the first is that the people were not worthy of so great a distinction in the eyes of HaShem, that He should destroy before them the inhabitants of the land — great and mighty nations — and even though He destroyed Egypt for their sake, one does not learn from Egypt to the inhabitants of the land, seven great and mighty nations, and the people of Israel were not so beloved before Him then as to destroy many nations for their sake. And the second is that HaShem desired the people and loved them, but His power did not suffice, perish the thought, against the inhabitants of the land. Therefore he said <b>they heard that you, HaShem, are in the midst,</b> etc. — meaning, they will not say that the cause that would arise from the inhabitants of the land is because they too are beloved and precious to the Creator, blessed be He, as has been mentioned; for they have heard of the belovedness of Israel before you, for you are HaShem in the midst of the people, that eye to eye, etc. — behold, their love for HaShem is extraordinary, and it is publicized that His great name is called upon them. And if He were able to do good for them, He would not refrain out of fear of the nations, which did not attain even a hundredth part of the love of Israel, which is revealed to all the world. And from now on, when You destroy this people, they will not attribute the matter to a deficiency in the reach of Your love for them, and if You do this thing, ״and You destroy, etc. and they will say,״ etc."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:59.183976355Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}